1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,281
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,281 --> 00:00:05,904
In this lesson, you'll learn to shape
your dashboard around the way you work.

3
00:00:05,904 --> 00:00:08,846
We'll resize and rearrange
widgets, add new ones,

4
00:00:08,846 --> 00:00:12,329
and build a separate dashboard
for each role in your team.

5
00:00:13,192 --> 00:00:16,978
The default dashboard is built
around your sales pipeline.

6
00:00:16,978 --> 00:00:18,806
That's perfect for an owner.

7
00:00:18,806 --> 00:00:23,897
But your receptionist cares about today's
appointments and tasks, not revenue.

8
00:00:23,897 --> 00:00:28,140
A good dashboard answers the
questions one person asks every day.

9
00:00:28,992 --> 00:00:32,801
To change a dashboard, click the
pencil icon at the top right.

10
00:00:32,801 --> 00:00:37,838
Each widget now shows a grip on the left
for moving it, a pencil for its settings,

11
00:00:37,838 --> 00:00:40,910
and a handle in the bottom
corner for resizing it.

12
00:00:41,759 --> 00:00:45,732
Let's make the funnel wider, so
the stage names have more room.

13
00:00:45,732 --> 00:00:48,003
Drag its corner handle to the right.

14
00:00:48,003 --> 00:00:52,606
The width snaps to a 12-column grid,
so everything stays neatly lined up.

15
00:00:53,457 --> 00:00:54,444
Next, rearrange.

16
00:00:54,444 --> 00:00:57,283
Put the number you check
most in the top left,

17
00:00:57,283 --> 00:00:59,875
because that's where your eye lands first.

18
00:00:59,875 --> 00:01:04,936
I'll drag conversion rate by its grip, and
drop it in front of opportunity status.

19
00:01:05,786 --> 00:01:08,007
Every widget has its own settings.

20
00:01:08,007 --> 00:01:12,385
Click its pencil to rename it,
choose which pipeline it reports on,

21
00:01:12,385 --> 00:01:14,149
or override the date range.

22
00:01:14,149 --> 00:01:17,743
I'll point conversion rate
at all pipelines, then save.

23
00:01:19,036 --> 00:01:21,508
To add something new, click Add widget.

24
00:01:21,508 --> 00:01:25,756
Widgets are grouped by area:
opportunities, appointments, contacts,

25
00:01:25,756 --> 00:01:27,087
tasks and reputation.

26
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:31,778
I'll add the appointments widget, which
shows bookings and your show rate.

27
00:01:32,629 --> 00:01:33,478
Happy with it?

28
00:01:33,478 --> 00:01:34,145
Click Save.

29
00:01:34,145 --> 00:01:39,119
If you change your mind while editing,
Cancel puts everything back the way it was.

30
00:01:39,119 --> 00:01:43,971
Remember that changes to a shared dashboard
show up for everyone who can see it,

31
00:01:43,971 --> 00:01:49,005
so if you just want to experiment, duplicate
it first, and play with your own copy.

32
00:01:49,856 --> 00:01:52,510
Now let's build a dashboard
for the front desk.

33
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:54,203
Click New, and give it a name.

34
00:01:54,203 --> 00:01:57,365
Start from a blank dashboard,
and choose who can see it.

35
00:01:57,365 --> 00:01:59,285
I'll share this one with everyone.

36
00:02:01,289 --> 00:02:03,441
It opens empty, and ready to edit.

37
00:02:03,441 --> 00:02:06,543
I'll add appointments,
tasks, and manual actions,

38
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:11,608
which lists the calls and texts your
workflows have queued for a person to make.

39
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,861
Save it, and it's ready.

40
00:02:13,861 --> 00:02:18,115
Anyone can now switch between dashboards
from the menu at the top left,

41
00:02:18,115 --> 00:02:21,950
and you can set the one you see
first, from the three dots menu.

42
00:02:25,075 --> 00:02:26,526
Not sure where to start?

43
00:02:26,526 --> 00:02:27,736
Here are some ideas.

44
00:02:27,736 --> 00:02:31,667
For the owner: opportunity value,
conversion rate and the funnel.

45
00:02:31,667 --> 00:02:35,236
For the front desk: appointments,
tasks and manual actions.

46
00:02:35,236 --> 00:02:38,865
And for whoever runs your
marketing: the lead source report,

47
00:02:38,865 --> 00:02:43,340
next to conversion rate, so they can
see which channels bring in patients,

48
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,489
not just enquiries.

49
00:02:45,339 --> 00:02:46,405
Here's a pro tip.

50
00:02:46,405 --> 00:02:51,173
Keep each dashboard to about five
widgets, and build it around one question,

51
00:02:51,173 --> 00:02:53,368
like: are we busy enough this week?

52
00:02:53,368 --> 00:02:56,756
If a widget never changes
what anyone does, remove it.

53
00:02:56,756 --> 00:02:58,826
A short dashboard gets looked at.

54
00:02:58,826 --> 00:03:00,331
A long one gets ignored.

55
00:03:01,195 --> 00:03:01,906
Great work!

56
00:03:01,906 --> 00:03:07,207
Next, we'll connect your ad accounts, and
see which campaigns turn into real leads

57
00:03:07,207 --> 00:03:08,307
and real revenue.

58
00:03:08,307 --> 00:03:10,052
See you in the next lesson.
